  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Use heterostructured square-lattice iridate superlattices to frustrate Neel antiferromagnetic order, measure quantum fluctuations with time-resolved RXD, and use polarization-resolved high-resolution RIXS to test whether conventional magnons are absent while broadband isotropic continua provide evidence for spinons in a quasi-two-dimensional square-lattice Heisenberg antiferromagnet setting and iridates provide a platform for exploring deconfined spin-1/2 spinons.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
